(18188,10,0,'%s grumbles under his breath.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Tatai'),
(18188,11,0,'T\'ink ja be contributin\' less glarin\' in dis troll\'s direction?',12,1,100,6,0,0,'Tatai'),
(18188,12,0,'%s sighs in resignation and falls silent.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Tatai'),
(18189,0,0,'This city is very... expansive, but it seems to be lacking something. I can\'t put my finger on what...',12,1,100,6,0,0,'Dela Runetotem'),
(18189,1,0,'It seems that a great deal of your power is used for... and I hope you\'ll pardon the term... frivolous things. Isn\'t that, well, wasteful?',12,1,100,6,0,0,'Dela Runetotem'),
(18189,2,0,'Tatai, please. We\'re guests here.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Dela Runetotem'),
(18189,3,0,'There\'s an ethereal beauty about this place... but for all the trees and plant life, it\'s still so... unnatural.',12,1,100,0,0,0,'Dela Runetotem'),
(18189,4,0,'As you say, ambassador. We can wait.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Dela Runetotem'),
(18189,5,0,'Tell us, Ambassador Kelemar... how do the blood elves plan to aid us, exactly?',12,1,100,6,0,0,'Dela Runetotem'),
(18189,6,0,'Dela Runetotem\'s brow furrows, but she remains silent.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Dela Runetotem'),
(18189,7,0,'My condolences. These past years have been hard on us all.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Dela Runetotem'),
(18190,0,0,'You\'re not the only victims of the Scourge. Our lady Sylvanas sympathizes with your plight.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Kristine Denny'),
(18190,1,0,'Your choice of decor is intriguing, Kelemar. Tell me - why the arcane frippery?',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Kristine Denny'),
(18190,2,0,'An understandable expenditure, as I see it. Show everyone, enemies and allies alike, that you\'re not afraid to use your power.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Kristine Denny'),
(18190,3,0,'Such marvelous sights. I regret being unable to see it when I was younger.',12,1,100,0,0,0,'Kristine Denny'),
(18190,4,0,'Truly an advantageous alliance.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Kristine Denny'),
(18190,5,0,'I thought we were going to speak with the regent lord. I\'m beginning to question whether or not he exists at all at this point.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Kristine Denny'),
(18190,6,0,'This is becoming tiresome.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Kristine Denny'),
(18190,7,0,'Troll, if you can\'t keep a civil tongue in your head, I\'ll be happy to remove it for you.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Kristine Denny'),
(18190,8,0,'%s smirks triumphantly.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Kristine Denny'),
(18191,0,0,'This is merely part of what Silvermoon once was. Much of the city was lost after Arthas swept through our lands.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Ambassador Kelemar'),
(18191,0,1,'We lost many of our kin in the war... so yes, the city is not perhaps as lively as it once was. We will endure, however.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Ambassador Kelemar'),
(18191,1,0,'It is not simply a beautification measure, but also a morale booster. It demonstrates to our people that we have a great deal of power at our fingertips, and with it... we can do nearly anything.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Ambassador Kelemar'),
(18191,2,0,'Think about it carefully, my friends. If we can afford to spend our magic on simple aesthetic enhancements, clearly we hold a vast reservoir of power at our beck and call.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Ambassador Kelemar'),
(18191,2,1,'This must be somewhat different from the environment to which you\'re accustomed. It is a visible demonstration of the power we hold, nothing more. We\'re mindful of our resources.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Ambassador Kelemar'),
(18191,3,0,'Yes, well... luckily for us all, the troll will not be in a position of power within our fair city anytime soon.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Ambassador Kelemar'),
(18191,4,0,'The regent lord is a very busy man. I\'m sure you understand.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Ambassador Kelemar'),
(18191,4,1,'He is unable to see you just yet, but do not trouble yourselves over it. I\'m certain he will find a way to fit you into his busy schedule.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Ambassador Kelemar'),
(18191,4,2,'In due course. There is no rush, after all - our hospitality is extended to you indefinitely. Even the troll.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Ambassador Kelemar'),
(18191,5,0,'Exercise caution during your stay. Some close-minded individuals may still cling to old alliances long since dissolved...',12,1,100,0,0,0,'Ambassador Kelemar'),
(18191,5,1,'Thank you for making the journey here. I hope you will find Silvermoon to your liking.',12,1,100,0,0,0,'Ambassador Kelemar'),
(18191,5,2,'Behold the wonders of our fair city.',12,1,100,0,0,0,'Ambassador Kelemar'),
(18191,6,0,'Our people are strong. We bring you a mastery over arcane magics that you have previously lacked - ah, no offense intended, of course.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Ambassador Kelemar'),
(18191,6,1,'Surely you see the advantage in our relationship. The powers we command are immense. With our aid, your enemies could well be decimated.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Ambassador Kelemar'),
(18191,6,2,'I realize we have had somewhat differing loyalties in the past, but put your suspicions aside. Our considerable power has been pledged to your leaders in good faith.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Ambassador Kelemar'),
(18191,7,0,'I\'m afraid your ancestry is the cause, troll. Decades of fighting with your green-skinned brethren have hardened their hearts against your kind.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Ambassador Kelemar'),
(18191,8,0,'Keep your chin up. Perhaps with time, our people will see you as the ally you are, rather than the enemy you appear to be.',12,1,100,1,0,0,'Ambassador Kelemar'),
(18200,0,0,'%s smiles and sheathes his rifle.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Shado \'Fitz\' Farstrider'),
(18218,1,0,'What\'s going on?!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Harold Lane'),
(18218,2,0,'Um... guys?',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Harold Lane'),
(18218,3,0,'Hemet?  Fitz?',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Harold Lane'),
(18218,4,0,'Oh good, I was beginning to worry.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Harold Lane'),
(18218,5,0,'Shifting, %s moans from the pain of his thorn scratch.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Harold Lane'),
(18218,5,1,'%s groans in pain.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Harold Lane'),
(18218,5,2,'%s looks at his friends and then grunts painfully.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Harold Lane'),
(18218,5,3,'%s wakes himself up snoring.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Harold Lane'),
(18218,5,4,'%s winces when he touches the tender area around his scratch.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Harold Lane'),
(18218,5,5,'%s begins to whistle a tune, but then stops abruptly and moans.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Harold Lane'),
(18230,0,0,'The magister\'s going to kill me...',12,1,100,0,0,0,'Trayanise'),
(18230,0,1,'No, no, no! Come back here!',12,1,100,0,0,0,'Trayanise'),
(18230,0,2,'Argh. They told me those crystals would work properly!',12,1,100,0,0,0,'Trayanise'),
(18230,0,3,'When I catch you, I\'m going to disenchant your components, so help me...',12,1,100,0,0,0,'Trayanise'),
(18230,0,4,'Get back here, you little...',12,1,100,0,0,0,'Trayanise'),
(18230,0,5,'You stay out of the regent lord\'s way! I mean it!',12,1,100,0,0,0,'Trayanise'),
(18248,0,0,'Grunting, %s turns away from the wanted poster, returning to his warm spot by the fire.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Nekthar'),
(18248,1,0,'%s begins to read the wanted poster.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Nekthar'),
(18265,0,0,'Nothing surprising there.  Come back with some real news, will you?',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Gezhe'),
(18265,0,1,'As expected.  Very well, dismissed.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Gezhe'),
(18274,0,0,'Try to keep appraisal errors to a minimum.  I\'d hate to tell Gezhe we\'ve overpaid on another gem shipment this month.',12,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(18294,0,0,'Hi, Harold.  I have your skins!',12,0,100,3,0,0,'Kristen Dipswitch'),
(18294,1,0,'Ack!  Somebody help me!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Kristen Dipswitch'),
(18302,0,0,'I will do my best to take care of the children, Greatmother.',12,0,100,0,0,0,''),
(18303,0,0,'My brothers and sisters. Listen to me. We must speak of the survival of our people. We have narrowly survived one calamity, but I fear the next shall destroy us.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Lyria Skystrider'),
(18303,1,0,'Can you not see what is happening? Open your eyes. It is laid bare for all to see. What is this new alliance? Why have we betrayed our allies of old, only to take up with the enemies of all that live?',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Lyria Skystrider'),
(18303,2,0,'You speak of her as friend? You are a fool. This "Dark Lady" is not Sylvanas.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Lyria Skystrider'),
(18303,3,0,'Blood? And these orcs, these fair weather friends? They will aid us?',12,0,100,11,0,0,'Lyria Skystrider'),
(18303,4,0,'The magisters are the traitors! They have sealed our doom.',12,0,100,25,0,0,'Lyria Skystrider'),
(18303,5,0,'We have not struggled so hard to survive, only to bring about the true destruction.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Lyria Skystrider'),
(18303,6,0,'If we speak as one, we cannot be ignored!',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Lyria Skystrider'),
(18303,7,0,'We will repay the betrayal of the Alliance! We shall never forget, and never forgive!',12,1,100,21,0,0,'Lyria Skystrider'),
(18327,0,0,'In Terokk\'s name!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Time-Lost Controller'),
(18327,0,1,'Protect the Veil!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Time-Lost Controller'),
(18327,0,2,'Darkfire -- avenge us!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Time-Lost Controller'),
(18327,0,3,'Ssssekk-sara Rith-nealaak!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Time-Lost Controller'),
(18327,0,4,'Arak-ha!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Time-Lost Controller'),
(18337,0,0,'That should take care of that. Summon me if you have further need of my services.',12,0,100,11,0,0,'Priest Kath\'mar'),
(18340,0,0,'I will show you not to cross us again!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Steam Pump Overseer'),
(18340,0,1,'Warlord Kalithresh will hear of this insolence!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Steam Pump Overseer'),
(18340,0,2,'I\'ll make you pay for that!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Steam Pump Overseer'),
(18384,0,0,'%s dons his wolf-fur vestments.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Malukaz'),
(18384,1,0,'Wolf spirit of the forest, hear me!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Malukaz'),
(18384,2,0,'Long ago, you were a companion to my people. We gave ourselves to evil and you were forgotten.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Malukaz'),
(18384,3,0,'But we have returned, spirit! We have returned to honor you again. Favor us with your presence once more.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Malukaz'),
(18384,4,0,'May our bond with you never be broken again, spirit.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Malukaz'),
(18384,5,0,'We have done it! Thrall would be proud.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Malukaz'),
(18408,0,0,'New posting going up! Adventurers and heroes, gather round the bulletin board!',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Warden Moi\'bff Jill'),
(18408,1,0,'That should get Telaar the assistance it needs!',12,7,100,5,0,0,'Warden Moi\'bff Jill'),
(18459,0,0,'Rejoice, my friends! $n has saved us from the looming shadow that threatened our very lives!',14,7,100,22,0,0,'Jenai Starwhisper'),
(18475,0,0,'Come out, little birdies! Mug\'gok want to play!',14,0,100,0,0,0,'Muggok'),
(18475,1,0,'No hurt Mug\'gok\'s feelings, bird-men!',14,0,100,0,0,0,'Muggok'),
(18475,2,0,'Fine! Birdies be dat way! Mug\'gok find new friends!',14,0,100,14,0,0,'Muggok'),
(18547,0,0,'We\'re rather selective of who we befriend, $n.  You think you have what it takes?',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Scryer Arcanist'),
(18596,0,0,'Are you joking?  I\'m a Scryer, I always watch what I say.  More enemies than allies in this city, it seems.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Arcanist Adyria'),
(18597,0,0,'A newcomer to Shattrath!  Make sure to drop by later.  We can always use a hand with the injured.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Sha\'nir'),
(18622,0,0,'Be mindful of what you say, this one\'s being shown around by Khadgar\'s pet.',12,0,100,0,0,0,'Iz\'zard'),
(18668,0,0,'No, you\'re wrong! We were the ones betrayed!',12,0,100,22,0,0,'Vaeron Kormar'),
(18668,1,0,'The Ranger-General of Silvermoon will be a loyal ally!',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Vaeron Kormar'),
(18668,2,0,'Blood will be true. We can trust in none but our own!',12,0,100,25,0,0,'Vaeron Kormar'),
(18668,3,0,'You call us traitors?',12,0,100,25,0,0,'Vaeron Kormar'),
(18669,0,0,'When have the dwarves ever been our friends?',12,0,100,11,0,0,'Terric Brightwind'),
(18669,1,0,'How are we to live without magic?',12,0,100,5,0,0,'Terric Brightwind'),
(18669,2,0,'Idealistic blather. Go back to your forests!',12,0,100,3,0,0,'Terric Brightwind'),
(18671,0,0,'You fool! The prince\'s minions were the very Forsaken we have now allied ourselves with, and now he has betrayed us!',12,0,100,5,0,0,'Priest Ennas'),
(18671,1,0,'A great blight lies across our land! It grows every day. Our need for magic weakens us, and will bring us to destruction, just as it has before!',12,0,100,25,0,0,'Priest Ennas'),
(18671,2,0,'But at what cost? You\'ve all been blinded. We have all been blinded.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Priest Ennas'),
(18671,3,0,'No, not savagery! Conscience. The excesses of our people will destroy us, and all that we have struggled to build.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Priest Ennas'),
(18671,4,0,'We stand on the brink of destruction. We must reconsider this rash course of action.',12,0,100,5,0,0,'Priest Ennas'),
(18671,5,0,'Lend us your voices! Now is the time we must act to save our people.',12,0,100,1,0,0,'Priest Ennas'),
(18671,6,0,'Lor\'themar must hear us! We will not be silenced!',12,0,100,5,0,0,'Priest Ennas'),
(18671,7,0,'Lor\'themar has remade Silvermoon into something we may truly be proud of.',12,1,100,21,0,0,'Priest Ennas'),
(18671,8,0,'The magisters are wise and will plot a prosperous course for our future.',12,1,100,21,0,0,'Priest Ennas'),
(18677,0,0,'%s becomes enraged!',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Mekthorg the Wild'),
(18679,0,0,'%s becomes enraged!',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Vorakem Doomspeaker'),
(18713,0,0,'Rifling through the stacks of books and scrolls on the table, Lieutenant Gravelhammer begins to examine one in particular with interest.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Lieutenant Gravelhammer'),
(18713,1,0,'What?  What\'s this?!',12,7,100,5,0,0,'Lieutenant Gravelhammer'),
(18713,1,1,'That is not even remotely imaginable!',12,7,100,5,0,0,'Lieutenant Gravelhammer');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `creature_text` (`entry`,`groupid`,`id`,`text`,`type`,`language`,`probability`,`emote`,`duration`,`sound`,`comment`) VALUES
(18713,1,2,'Looks like I picked a bad day to stop drinking.',12,7,100,5,0,0,'Lieutenant Gravelhammer'),
(18713,1,3,'How did this get missed?!',12,7,100,5,0,0,'Lieutenant Gravelhammer'),
(18713,2,0,'Cap\'n, sir, we have a slight problem.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Lieutenant Gravelhammer'),
(18713,3,0,'As you say, sir.  It would appear that someone failed to mention to me that the druids at the Cenarion Thicket have been wiped out!',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Lieutenant Gravelhammer'),
(18713,3,1,'Bad news.  We\'ve been hit again.  They\'re gone, but the front sentry tower is on fire.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Lieutenant Gravelhammer'),
(18713,3,2,'One of our merchants has gone missing!',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Lieutenant Gravelhammer'),
(18713,3,3,'That group that recently arrived from Honor Hold -- they\'re mercs!  They\'re starting to stir up trouble.  Maybe I should have a talk with them?',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Lieutenant Gravelhammer'),
(18713,3,4,'One of our scouts is reporting that a shadowy group has moved into the ruins of Grangol\'var Village.  Oops, this report is over a week old.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Lieutenant Gravelhammer'),
(18713,3,5,'We have reports from a scout in the field that one of the Cenarion druids has been taken captive up at Firewing Point.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Lieutenant Gravelhammer'),
(18713,4,0,'Aye, aye, sir.  Right away!',12,7,100,66,0,0,'Lieutenant Gravelhammer'),
(18724,0,0,'The humans abandoned us in our darkest hour! Their prince himself led the assault on our lands.',12,0,100,25,0,0,'Melaya Tassier'),
(18724,1,0,'Look at the wonders of this city! This is magic.',12,0,100,5,0,0,'Melaya Tassier'),
(18724,2,0,'You would have us live like the savages!',12,0,100,5,0,0,'Melaya Tassier'),
(18745,5,0,'At ease, lieutenant. Go on.',12,7,100,66,0,0,'Captain Auric Sunchaser'),
(18745,5,1,'What is it now, Gravel?',12,7,100,6,0,0,'Captain Auric Sunchaser'),
(18745,5,2,'What else could possibly go wrong?',12,7,100,6,0,0,'Captain Auric Sunchaser'),
(18745,5,3,'Yes, lieutenant?  Report.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Captain Auric Sunchaser'),
(18745,6,0,'That\'s troubling news indeed.  See to it that it\'s taken care of immediately!',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Captain Auric Sunchaser'),
(18745,6,1,'I don\'t have time for this, lieutenant.  Make sure that you handle it.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Captain Auric Sunchaser'),
(18745,6,2,'If we\'re to help with that in any way we\'ll need more people.  Call some of the scouts in to help with that.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Captain Auric Sunchaser'),
(18745,6,3,'Lieutenant, I want you to make that your top priority.  Notify anyone that you think can help.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Captain Auric Sunchaser'),
(18810,0,0,'How can you have any pudding if you don\'t eat your fish?',12,7,100,5,0,0,'Otonambusi'),
(18810,0,1,'If you don\'t eat your fish, you can\'t have any pudding!',12,7,100,5,0,0,'Otonambusi'),
(18823,0,0,'What about the earth spirits?',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Minor Water Spirit'),
(18827,0,0,'%s\'s eyes glow red as he begins to cackle madly!.',16,7,100,0,0,0,'Gan\'arg Sapper'),
(18897,0,0,'Welcome, welcome, to the recently appropriated and callously renamed Steamwheedle Stadium!',12,0,100,0,0,0,'"King" Dond'),
(18904,0,0,'Turn back, mortal... This is not your battle.',15,0,100,0,0,0,'Vision of the Forgotten'),
(18904,0,1,'You cannot stop them...',15,0,100,0,0,0,'Vision of the Forgotten'),
(18904,0,2,'We are infinite... eternal.',15,0,100,0,0,0,'Vision of the Forgotten'),
(18904,0,3,'They lack control... Oshu\'gun calls to them...',15,0,100,0,0,0,'Vision of the Forgotten'),
(18904,0,4,'It is a beacon. A remnant of a forgotten era.',15,0,100,0,0,0,'Vision of the Forgotten'),
(18917,0,0,'%s chuckles softly.',16,0,100,11,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,1,0,'The earth spirits are very much present in this chamber, my child. After all, we are underground, are we not?',12,7,100,6,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,2,0,'They are stoic, the spirits of the earth. Through them, the shaman learns to endure the hardships of life.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,3,0,'The rocks are here when we first enter this world, and they will remain long after we pass.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,4,0,'Stand... there is more to discuss.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,5,0,'Stop here a moment, my children, and close your eyes. Can you feel the air currents?',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,6,0,'The two students close their eyes and bow their heads.',16,7,100,0,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,7,0,'The spirits of the air can be found even here, underground. They dislike being surrounded, constricted by the earth... their precious freedom is limited here.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,8,0,'They are flighty, these spirits, and easily distracted... but they will share their secrets with those who know how to listen.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,9,0,'%s smiles to himself as he watches the students fidget in their concentration.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,10,0,'Come. There is more to study than the secrets on the wind.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,11,0,'Can you feel the warmth here, my children?',12,7,100,6,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,12,0,'The students nod slowly, eyes rapt on their teacher.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,13,0,'Focus upon that warmth as I speak...',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,14,0,'The strength of fire lies in change. Its strength is considerable, but ever-shifting... unpredictable.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,15,0,'This is extended to the spirits themselves. They are often quick to anger; it is important thet you learn to listen without falling prey to their tempers.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,16,0,'That is enough for now. Come.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,17,0,'The water here is peaceful, is it not? Listening to the trickle from the ceiling can aid you in finding its true voice...',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,18,0,'The water spirits are perhaps the most outspoken. They are generous and understanding. Indeed, if you are having trouble hearing the voices, it is with water that you should begin.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,19,0,'Close your eyes, my children, and listen to the water within these halls.',12,7,100,1,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,20,0,'Both students close their eyes, straining to hear the voices.',16,0,100,0,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,21,0,'%s nods to himself and clears his throat.',16,0,100,273,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18917,22,0,'Stand, my children... that\'s enough for now.',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Chakaa'),
(18918,0,0,'Yes, teacher.',12,7,100,273,0,0,'Drysc'),
(18927,0,0,'Legend says that the great beast Omen sleeps in the waters of Lake Elune\'ara in Moonglade, only to appear once a year. But that\'s just a legend.',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Human Commoner to Human Commoner'),
(18927,0,1,'Have you seen the fireworks? This is the best time of year to buy them.',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Human Commoner to Human Commoner'),
(18927,0,2,'The druids of Nighthaven are holding a great celebration in Moonglade for the Lunar Festival.',12,7,100,0,0,0,'Human Commoner to Human Commoner'),
(18927,0,3,'Legend says that the great beast Omen sleeps in the waters of Lake Elune\'ara in Moonglade, only to appear once a year. But that\'s just a legend.',12,7,100,274,0,0,'Human Commoner to Human Commoner'),
(18927,0,4,'The druids of Nighthaven are holding a great celebration in Moonglade for the Lunar Festival.',12,7,100,274,0,0,'Human Commoner to Human Commoner'),
